Let the interface wifili hands a decapped frame to be chosen at load time
rather than fixed at the ethernet receive node.

The ethernet receive node delivers to the host. The EDMA node transmits a
frame with no destination port set, which is the descriptor the firmware
builds when the PPE is to process a frame rather than forward it to a
port, so a frame handed there enters the PPE ingress pipeline and is
matched against the flow tables.

The default is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
index 0ecdab4..82ef9f6 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -14,6 +14,16 @@
 #include "wmi.h"
 #include "../../../../../net/mac80211/sta_info.h"
 
+/* Interface the firmware hands a decapped frame to once wifili is done with it.
+ * The ethernet receive node is the one that reaches the host; the EDMA node
+ * transmits with no destination port, which puts the frame through the PPE
+ * ingress pipeline instead.
+ */
+static bool nss_edma_next_hop;
+module_param(nss_edma_next_hop, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(nss_edma_next_hop,
+		 "deliver wifili frames to the EDMA node instead of the host");
+
 /*-----------------------------ATH11K-NSS Helpers--------------------------*/
 
 static enum ath11k_nss_opmode
@@ -3590,8 +3600,10 @@ int ath11k_nss_setup(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 		goto pdev_deinit;
 	}
 
-	/* Default nexthop interface is set to ETH RX */
-	ret = nss_wifi_vdev_base_set_next_hop(ab->nss.ctx, NSS_ETH_RX_INTERFACE);
+	ret = nss_wifi_vdev_base_set_next_hop(ab->nss.ctx,
+					      nss_edma_next_hop ?
+					      NSS_EDMA_INTERFACE :
+					      NSS_ETH_RX_INTERFACE);
 	if (ret != NSS_TX_SUCCESS) {
 		ath11k_warn(ab, "Failure to set default next hop : %d\n", ret);
 		goto stop;
